          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Page no. 236"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.51,
            0.881,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In each case, the angles are the multiples of the smallest angle. You may wonder and ask if this will always happen. What do you think?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.557,
            0.881,
            0.593
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Yes, the angles of symmetry are always the multiples of the smallest angle. For example, the second angle is twice the amount of rotation of the first rotation."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.626,
            0.147,
            0.647
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 17,
              "bbox": [
                0.118,
                0.626,
                0.147,
                0.647
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_35_image_17.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.119,
            0.628,
            0.276,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "True or False"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.659,
            0.698,
            0.677
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Every figure will have 360 degrees as an angle of symmetry.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.147,
            0.678,
            0.882,
            0.712
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "If the smallest angle of symmetry of a figure is a natural number in degrees, then it is a factor of 360.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 21,
          "bbox": [
            0.146,
            0.723,
            0.284,
            0.74
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ans.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " True"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 22,
          "bbox": [
            0.237,
            0.75,
            0.284,
            0.766
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "True"
            }
          ]
        },
